Abstract

This study evaluates EGFR-directed therapy in advanced solid tumours and reports
survival outcomes across a multicentre cohort.

Introduction

Targeted degradation has reshaped treatment. Prior work established feasibility.

Methods

Patients were enrolled prospectively. Eligibility required confirmed mutation.

1. Statistical Analysis

Cox models estimated hazard ratios with two-sided tests at alpha 0.05.

Results

The treatment arm showed a hazard ratio of 0.62 versus control.

Conclusions

EGFR-directed therapy improved survival in this cohort.
